\details{
\strong{T scores.} Each scale's T score is
\code{50 + 10 * (score - M) / SD}, with the scale's \code{M} and \code{SD} from
\link{hitopdat_norms}, rounded to a whole number with halves rounded away
from zero. Both of the authors' versions of the battery round T scores
to whole numbers. A score of \code{NA} gives a T score of \code{NA}. The norms and
their sources are:
\itemize{
\item WHODAS: Andrews et al. (2009), Table 1, the total row and column.
\item The 18 IDAS-II scales: Watson et al. (2012), Table 2, the "Adults"
column.
\item CAPE positive symptoms: Galletly et al. (2016), Table 1, the men's and
women's means weighted by their n, with the SD printed for both,
divided by the 20 items.
\item The 33 CAT-PD facets: the "Community" means and SDs of Len Simms's
CAT-PD and IDAS scoring workbook. These norms are unpublished. The
battery's authors use them, and this function follows the authors.
}

The AUDIT, DUDIT and PHQ-15 get no T score yet. Their norms are split by
